  "experiment_id": "EXP-FP-0100",
  "hypothesis": "Estimand re-scoping (exclude the pure-RNG cue channels from the estimand; competence = predictable error) couples the causal online competence estimator to error magnitude: Brier beats sequential climatology on >=3/4 domains AND corr(predicted_uncertainty, predictable|err|) >= 0.40 on the re-scoped D1/D3 estimand.",
  "interpretation": "NULL_HOLDS (family 1 of the post-0072 re-scoping program): estimand re-scoping does NOT make the estimator win. Brier beats climatology on 2/4 only: D2 action_consequence 0.25036 vs 0.25063 (marginal, CALIBRATED verdict -- beats AND ECE/MCE in gates) and D4 retrieval_usefulness 0.24248 vs 0.24403 (marginal); D1 next_obs 0.24962 vs 0.24851 LOSES and D3 competence_failure 0.11492 vs 0.11484 LOSES on the re-scoped rest events. Coupling corr(predicted_uncertainty, predictable|err|): 0.026/0.069/0.083/0.060 -- 0/4 reach 0.40; the gated D1/D3 coupling is 0.026 and 0.083, no better than the total-error arc. The honest expectation was stated up front (batch oracle R^2=0.078 -> corr 0.28 with the tested features) and the data land exactly there: even on the predictable component, the available causal features carry ~7% of the variance, and no coupling. The reference arm is decisive: the 0072 variant-C estimator, replayed on the same logs and scored on the same re-scoped estimand, posts essentially IDENTICAL numbers (D1 0.25072 vs 0.24851, corr 0.032; D3 0.11499 vs 0.11484, corr 0.076; D2/D4 identical) -- the estimand change + p-head retraining added nothing over the total-error estimator. The signal ceiling extends to the re-scoped estimand: the predictable remainder is dominated by fast re-learning transients and 10% reward-noise flips, neither visible in any causal prediction-time feature tested. Families 2-3 are NOT run (conditional on family 1's win; nothing to generalize).",
